  "status_alias_evidence": "Monday status label index 4 carried 'Ready To Sent' (2026-02-02..2026-05-12), 'ready to sent' (2026-05-12..2026-06-07) and 'Ready To Send' (2026-06-07..) in consecutive, non-overlapping periods; index 13 carried 'Creat File' once (2026-02-18) then 'Create File'. Aliases apply only when the label index matches. Reused indexes (8 Uploading -> Captions Revisions, 10 Coloring -> Captions In Progress, 12 Downloaded -> Ready For Review, 14 Editing Now -> Waiting For Captions) are NOT aliased. See docs/evidence/REAL-001-STATUS.md.",
  "unmapped_previous_status": "accept-with-unresolved-previous",
  "unmapped_status_policy": "an entry into a mapped status is kept with the unmapped or cleared previous label preserved raw and from_status null; transitions into unmapped labels are quarantined (UNKNOWN_STATUS) and a cycle whose window (item's first status event through Ready For Approval) contains one is excluded from speed and deadline metrics; transitions into a cleared status are quarantined as STATUS_CLEARED and flagged only",
